      "id": "isthmus_7702_delegated_sender_transfer",
      "comment": "AUTH (addr4) already has 7702-delegated code installed *before* this vector's own tx runs (pre-seeded directly into `pre`, simulating a delegation installed by some earlier tx/block -- op-geth's EIP-7702 does not disqualify a delegated EOA from being a tx sender). AUTH itself sends a completely ordinary EIP-1559 transfer (no setcode tx involved this time -- exercises the existing eip1559 tx path, not the new setcode one). Checks that fee buying / nonce checks / value transfer all work normally for a sender whose account has non-empty (delegation-indicator) code, exactly as they would for a plain EOA.",
